        <h3>Why become a mentor?</h3>
        <p>Becoming a mentor is not just rewarding for the person you guide, but it’s a transformative experience for you as well. Here are some key reasons why mentoring is such a great endeavor:</p>
        <p><strong>Making a Difference:</strong> You have the chance to positively impact someone's life by sharing your knowledge, experience, and wisdom. Watching someone grow and succeed because of your guidance is incredibly fulfilling.</p>
        <p><strong>Personal Growth:</strong> Mentoring often deepens your own understanding of your field or skills. It challenges you to communicate effectively, think critically, and reflect on your own journey.</p>
        <p><strong>Strengthening Leadership Skills:</strong> As a mentor, you develop abilities like patience, active listening, empathy, and strategic thinking—all of which are invaluable in personal and professional settings.</p>
        <p><strong>Creating a Legacy:</strong> Helping someone succeed creates a ripple effect; your impact extends beyond just one person. It’s a way to pass on what you've learned and leave a lasting contribution.</p>
        <p><strong>Building Relationships:</strong> Mentorship fosters deep connections, often leading to mutually enriching relationships that can last a lifetime.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Column 2 with custom gap -->
      <div class="col-sm-6 col-md-5">
        <h3>Why become a mentee?</h3>
        <p>Becoming a mentee is an incredible opportunity for personal and professional growth. Here’s why it can be so beneficial:</p>
        <p><strong>Learning from Experience:</strong> A mentor has often walked the path you're on and can share insights, lessons, and strategies to help you navigate challenges and avoid common pitfalls.</p>
        <p><strong>Expanding Your Perspective:</strong> Mentors can introduce you to new ideas, ways of thinking, or approaches you may not have considered, broadening your horizons.</p>
        <p><strong>Accelerating Your Development:</strong> With their guidance, you can progress more quickly in your goals, gaining valuable knowledge and skills at a faster pace.</p>
        <p><strong>Building Confidence:</strong> A mentor's encouragement and feedback can boost your self-assurance and motivate you to take on new challenges.</p>
        <p><strong>Networking Opportunities:</strong> Mentors often have extensive networks and can connect you to people, resources, or opportunities that align with your goals.</p>
        <p><strong>Personalized Guidance:</strong> Unlike general advice, a mentor's support is tailored to your unique aspirations, strengths, and areas for improvement.</p>
      </div>
